#### \(R_{aa}\)

The formula for calculating \(R_{AA}\) is given in Equation 5.4.

\[R_{AA}=\frac{\frac{1}{N_{mbAA}}\frac{dN_{AA}^{\Upsilon}}{dy}}{\frac{N_{bin}}{ \sigma_{pp}}\frac{d\sigma_{pp}^{\Upsilon}}{dy}} \tag{5.4}\]

Where \(N_{mbAA}\) is the number of minbias events from the luminosity sampled, \(\frac{dN_{AA}^{\Upsilon}}{dy}\) is the number of \(\Upsilon\) from the luminosity sampled, \(N_{\rm bin}\) is the average number of binary collisions in the centrality bin under investigation, \(\sigma_{pp}\) is the total inelastic p+p cross section which is taken to be 42 \(mb\) at \(\sqrt{s_{NN}}=200\ {\rm GeV}\). Finally, \(\frac{d\sigma_{pp}^{\Upsilon}}{dy}\) is the \(\Upsilon(1S+2S+3S)\) cross section measured in \(p+p\) collisions at \(\sqrt{s}=200\ {\rm GeV}\).

